---
title: Tooltips and Focus
description: Configure grouped focus, crosshairs, automatic content, ordering, placement, portaling, pinning, and framework-composed tooltip bodies.
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The DOM host provides a small automatic path for the common case:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"find the nearest chart point;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"draw a focus marker;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"show locale-aware text;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"expose the same point to pointer and keyboard users;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"notify typed application callbacks."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use that path until the product needs richer interaction."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"default-nearest-point","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default nearest point"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import the built-in tooltip extension and add it to the definition:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\n\nconst interactiveDefinition = defineChart(definition, { tooltip })\n\nconst host = mountChart(element, {\n  definition: interactiveDefinition,\n  height: 320,\n  ariaLabel: 'Weekly downloads',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default focus strategy resolves one nearest point in two dimensions.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxFocusDistance"},{"type":"text","value":" defaults to 48 scene pixels. Empty space farther from any\npoint clears transient focus."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"axis-focus-modes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Axis focus modes"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mode"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"omitted"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One nearest painted geometry or point in two dimensions"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nearest-x"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The containing mark, otherwise one point prioritizing x distance"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nearest-y"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The containing mark, otherwise one point prioritizing y distance"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group-x"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The containing mark first, plus its semantic x group; otherwise nearest x"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group-y"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The containing mark first, plus its semantic y group; otherwise nearest y"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grouped focus is appropriate for comparing several series at the same date or\ncategory. A sparse snapped cursor can opt into\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxFocusDistance: Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY"},{"type":"text","value":"; keep the finite default when\nempty space should mean no focus."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"angular-focus","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Angular focus"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusGroupAngle"},{"type":"text","value":" for the radial equivalent of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group-x"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineChart, type ChartDefinition } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { focusGroupAngle } from '@tanstack/charts/polar'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\n\ndeclare const radialDefinition: ChartDefinition\n\nconst interactiveDefinition = defineChart(radialDefinition, {\n  focus: focusGroupAngle,\n  tooltip,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The nearest radial ray selects the semantic angle, the closest radius becomes\nprimary, and the tooltip receives one point per series at that angle. The\nstrategy uses the same finite "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxFocusDistance"},{"type":"text","value":" policy as axis grouping.\nOrdinary pie and donut charts can keep default nearest focus: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"radialArc"},{"type":"text","value":"\nattaches the exact painted slice geometry, including the donut hole."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"primary"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group"},{"type":"text","value":" presentation follows the canonical focused scene\npoints. Equal x/y/series values in another facet do not implicitly paint a\nsecond focus marker. To synchronize a visual cursor across facets without\nturning those mirrors into additional selected data, add an ordinary focus\nmark with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"whenFocused(..., { match: 'x' })"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"match: 'y'"},{"type":"text","value":". The tooltip and\nfocus callback still receive the resolver's primary point or explicit focus\ngroup."}]},{"type":"code","value":"whenFocused(bandX(rows, { x: 'date' }), { match: 'x' })\nwhenFocused(bandY(rows, { y: 'value' }), { match: 'y' })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These are presentation filters, not alternate selection strategies. The first\npaints a vertical band wherever the focused x value exists; the second paints a\nhorizontal band wherever the focused y value exists. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"whenFocused"},{"type":"text","value":" can only\nreveal geometry already emitted by its authored mark. It cannot move one\nstable band between values."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the data-less "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"crosshair"},{"type":"text","value":" mark when one renderer-native guide should follow\nthe active focus instead of revealing authored geometry for a matching datum:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"live-example","tagName":"md-live-example","attributes":{"id":"focused-crosshair-1"},"properties":{"data-example-group":"focused-crosshair","data-collapsed-indexes":"[1]","data-workspace":"{\"version\":1,\"entry\":\"/src/chart.ts\",\"environment\":\"charts\",\"files\":{\"/src/chart.ts\":\"import { defineChart, lineY } from '@tanstack/charts'\\nimport { crosshair } from '@tanstack/charts/crosshair'\\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\\nimport { scalePoint } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/point'\\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\\nimport { rows } from './data'\\n\\nexport default defineChart({\\n  marks: [\\n    lineY(rows, {\\n      x: 'week',\\n      y: 'value',\\n      points: true,\\n      stroke: '#2563eb',\\n      strokeWidth: 2.5,\\n    }),\\n    crosshair({ x: { label: true }, y: false }),\\n  ],\\n  scales: {\\n    x: { scale: () => scalePoint<string>().padding(0.2) },\\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear, grid: true, axis: { label: 'Active users' } },\\n  },\\n\\n  focus: 'nearest-x',\\n  maxFocusDistance: Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY,\\n  tooltip,\\n})\",\"/src/data.ts\":\"export const rows = [\\n  { week: 'May 4', value: 820 },\\n  { week: 'May 11', value: 960 },\\n  { week: 'May 18', value: 1_140 },\\n  { week: 'May 25', value: 1_280 },\\n  { week: 'Jun 1', value: 1_210 },\\n  { week: 'Jun 8', value: 1_390 },\\n]\"}}"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { defineChart, lineY } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { crosshair } from '@tanstack/charts/crosshair'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\nimport { scalePoint } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/point'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\nimport { rows } from './data'\n\nexport default defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    lineY(rows, {\n      x: 'week',\n      y: 'value',\n      points: true,\n      stroke: '#2563eb',\n      strokeWidth: 2.5,\n    }),\n    crosshair({ x: { label: true }, y: false }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: () => scalePoint<string>().padding(0.2) },\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear, grid: true, axis: { label: 'Active users' } },\n  },\n\n  focus: 'nearest-x',\n  maxFocusDistance: Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY,\n  tooltip,\n})","lang":"ts","meta":"group=focused-crosshair env=charts file=/src/chart.ts entry","title":"/src/chart.ts","file":"/src/chart.ts"},{"type":"code","value":"export const rows = [\n  { week: 'May 4', value: 820 },\n  { week: 'May 11', value: 960 },\n  { week: 'May 18', value: 1_140 },\n  { week: 'May 25', value: 1_280 },\n  { week: 'Jun 1', value: 1_210 },\n  { week: 'Jun 8', value: 1_390 },\n]","lang":"ts","meta":"group=focused-crosshair file=/src/data.ts collapsed","title":"/src/data.ts","file":"/src/data.ts"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The vertical rule follows pointer and keyboard focus. The infinite distance is\nan explicit continuous-snapping policy; keep the finite default when empty\nspace should clear focus."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"crosshair"},{"type":"text","value":" defaults to both axis rules with no labels or marker. Setting\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"band: true"},{"type":"text","value":" or a band options object replaces that axis rule; axes with zero\nbandwidth emit no band. Guides are clipped to the plot and labels are clamped\nto the surface. They do not change nearest-point selection, add hit targets,\nor suppress the primary focus ring. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusRing: false"},{"type":"text","value":" only when authored\ncursor geometry deliberately replaces the ring. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../reference/focus-and-interaction.md#crosshair-guides","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Focus and Interaction"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nfor the complete band paint contract and controlled cursor behavior."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://tanstack.com/charts/catalog/119-stacked-bar-band-cursor/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Open the stacked cursor-band catalog case"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"automatic-tooltip-mapping","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Automatic tooltip mapping"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tooltip"},{"type":"text","value":" extension renders labeled rows for the focused point.\nGrouped focus uses the shared axis value as a heading and renders one row and\ncolor swatch per series. Visible axis labels carry into the tooltip. Numbers\nuse the user's locale and dates use stable UTC ISO formatting."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rect and link endpoints display as ranges. Bars and areas with an explicit\nbaseline display the interval length, so a stacked segment reports its own\nvalue instead of the cumulative endpoint."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Order built-in channels, datum fields, and derived text for a single focused\npoint:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const definition = defineChart({\n  marks,\n  scales: {\n    x: x,\n    y: y,\n  },\n\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    items: [\n      {\n        channel: 'y',\n        label: 'Revenue',\n        text: (point) => currency(point.yValue),\n      },\n      {\n        field: 'status',\n        label: 'Status',\n      },\n      {\n        id: 'change',\n        label: 'Change',\n        text: (point, { pinned }) =>\n          pinned && point.datum.change != null\n            ? percent(point.datum.change)\n            : null,\n      },\n      'x',\n    ],\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Array order is row order. A nullish field or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text"},{"type":"text","value":" result omits the row.\nItem "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"content"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"format"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"formatGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" callbacks receive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pinned"},{"type":"text","value":",\nwhich is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" during transient inspection and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" after click, Enter, or\nSpace.\nUse it to keep the transient tooltip compact and reveal detailed rows when the\nsame tooltip is pinned.\nGrouped focus keeps its shared-axis heading and series rows. By default, rows\nfollow the marks top-to-bottom for an x-group and left-to-right for a y-group.\nOverride that with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sort: 'color-domain'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sort: 'focus'"},{"type":"text","value":", or a typed\ncomparator. Use channel items to format their heading, series names, and values.\nUse "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"content"},{"type":"text","value":" when a grouped tooltip needs additional columns or nested\nsections."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Customize plaintext content with typed formatters:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const formattedDefinition = defineChart(definition, {\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    format(point, { pinned }) {\n      const suffix = pinned ? ' · pinned' : ''\n      return `${point.datum.label}: ${point.datum.value.toLocaleString()}${suffix}`\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For grouped focus:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const groupedDefinition = defineChart(definition, {\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    formatGroup(points, { pinned }) {\n      const date = points[0]?.xValue\n      const heading =\n        date instanceof Date ? date.toLocaleDateString() : String(date ?? '')\n\n      return [\n        pinned ? `${heading} · pinned` : heading,\n        ...points.map(\n          (point) =>\n            `${point.groupLabel}: ${point.datum.value.toLocaleString()}`,\n        ),\n      ].join('\\n')\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Formatting precedence is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"content"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"formatGroup"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"format"},{"type":"text","value":", then the automatic\ncontent. All three callbacks receive the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartTooltipContentContext"},{"type":"text","value":".\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"content"},{"type":"text","value":" returns safe title and row data. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"format"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"formatGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" return\nplain text; returning HTML does not create DOM."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"className"},{"type":"text","value":" to style the native HTML surface. Clicking pins the current\ntooltip for text selection. A later click or Escape unpins it. Set\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sticky: false"},{"type":"text","value":" to disable pinning."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"visibility: 'pinned'"},{"type":"text","value":" when focus should style the chart without opening a\ntransient tooltip. Click, Enter, or Space can still pin the focused point; only\nthe pinned surface and adapter body are mounted. The default is\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"visibility: 'focus'"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tooltip-motion","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tooltip motion"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The built-in tooltip uses the active motion renderer's transition for entry,\nmovement between points, retargeting, and exit:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { motion } from '@tanstack/charts/motion'\n\nconst renderer = motion({\n  transition: {\n    type: 'spring',\n    stiffness: 170,\n    damping: 18,\n    mass: 1,\n  },\n})\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks,\n  scales: {\n    x: null,\n    y: null,\n  },\n  tooltip,\n})\n\nmountChartRenderer(container, {\n  definition,\n  renderer,\n  width: 640,\n  height: 360,\n  ariaLabel: 'Monthly visitors',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A static chart-level transition can refine the renderer fallback:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const definition = defineChart({\n  marks,\n  scales: {\n    x: null,\n    y: null,\n  },\n  motion: {\n    transition: { type: 'spring', stiffness: 170, damping: 18, mass: 1 },\n  },\n  tooltip,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tooltip.motion"},{"type":"text","value":" to another transition to override both, or set it to\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" to keep the tooltip immediate. These options customize the active\nmotion renderer; a static renderer stays immediate and does not import spring\nphysics. The renderer's reduced-motion policy also applies to the tooltip."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For fast pointer inspection alongside slower data animation, set\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tooltip: { use: tooltip, motion: false }"},{"type":"text","value":", or give the tooltip a short tween:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const tooltipOptions = {\n  use: tooltip,\n  motion: { transition: { type: 'tween', duration: 120 } },\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inline mark "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"states"},{"type":"text","value":" wait for active entrance and data motion to finish.\nTooltips and separate focus marks continue updating during that time. See\nthe "},{"type":"link","href":"../reference/motion.md#motion","children":[{"type":"text","value":"motion reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for an immediate\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"whenFocused"},{"type":"text","value":" dot example."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"application-owned-pointer-timing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Application-owned pointer timing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set definition "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pointer: false"},{"type":"text","value":" when the application decides when inspection\nbegins, such as after a touch hold. Resolve the event and paint focus through\nthe controller exposed by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"host.interaction"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onRender"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const target = interaction.resolvePointer(event.clientX, event.clientY)\ninteraction.setControlledFocus(target)\n\n// On release or cancellation\ninteraction.setControlledFocus(null)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This keeps focus marks and tooltip content in the definition. The controller\nuses presentation points, so an active path motion or viewport translation\ndoes not detach the focus marker and tooltip from the painted datum. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./interactions-and-selections.md#controlled-point-inspection","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Controlled point inspection"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nfor the complete ownership boundary."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"anchoring-and-placement","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Anchoring and placement"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Point anchoring is the stable default for scatterplots, bars, and keyboard\nnavigation:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const pointDefinition = defineChart(definition, {\n  tooltip: { use: tooltip, anchor: 'point', placement: 'top' },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pointer anchoring is useful when a dense mark has a large interactive\nprimitive. Keyboard focus falls back to the primary point:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const pointerDefinition = defineChart(definition, {\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    anchor: 'pointer',\n    placement: ['right', 'left', 'bottom', 'top'],\n    offset: 12,\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grouped charts can avoid jumping between series by anchoring to the focused\ngroup's bounding-box center:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const definition = defineChart({\n  marks,\n  scales: {\n    x: x,\n    y: y,\n  },\n\n  focus: 'group-x',\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    anchor: 'group-center',\n    placement: ['top', 'right', 'left', 'bottom'],\n    sort: 'color-domain',\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Coordinates can be selected independently. This follows the focused x value\nwhile fixing the tooltip to the top of the plot:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const fixedYDefinition = defineChart(definition, {\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    anchor: { x: 'value', y: 'plot-top' },\n    placement: 'bottom',\n    offset: 12,\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A custom resolver covers event ranges, maps, and application-specific\nreference positions:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const customAnchorDefinition = defineChart(definition, {\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    anchor: (_points, { focus, pointer, plot, surface, scales }) => ({\n      x: (scales.x.viewport?.map ?? scales.x.map)(focus.primary.xValue),\n      y: plot.y,\n    }),\n    placement: 'bottom-left',\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resolvers receive complete focus, pointer, plot, surface, and resolved-scale\nstate. Resolvers and placement use scene pixels. A nullish or non-finite custom\nanchor falls back to the primary point. A placement list uses the first fit,\nthen the least-overflowing candidate."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"escaping-clipped-containers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Escaping clipped containers"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep tooltip layering with the chart definition:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { portal } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip/portal'\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks,\n  scales: {\n    x: x,\n    y: y,\n  },\n\n  focus: 'group-x',\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    portal,\n    anchor: 'group-center',\n    placement: ['right', 'left', 'bottom', 'top'],\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"portal"},{"type":"text","value":" extension opens the tooltip as a manual Popover in the browser top\nlayer where supported. It remains a DOM descendant of the chart, so inherited\nstyles, ancestor selectors, and chart-scoped CSS custom properties continue to\nwork. If Popover is unavailable or fails, the host moves the tooltip directly\nunder the chart's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ownerDocument"},{"type":"text","value":" body with fixed high-stack positioning. Both\npaths escape "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"overflow: hidden"},{"type":"text","value":" and local stacking contexts, use viewport\ncollision bounds, and reposition after scroll, viewport resize, or content\nresize. Omitting "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"portal"},{"type":"text","value":" keeps ordinary absolute positioning inside the chart."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For consistent fallback styling, target "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tooltip.className"},{"type":"text","value":" from a\ndocument-level stylesheet and define required CSS custom properties on that\nclass or a shared document ancestor."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"typed-callbacks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Typed callbacks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use callbacks when application UI needs the current semantic state:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function WeeklyDownloads() {\n  const groupedDefinition = defineChart(definition, { focus: 'group-x' })\n\n  return (\n    <Chart\n      definition={groupedDefinition}\n      ariaLabel=\"Weekly downloads\"\n      onFocusChange={(point) => {\n        setFocusedRow(point?.datum ?? null)\n      }}\n      onFocusGroupChange={(points) => {\n        setFocusedRows(points.map((point) => point.datum))\n      }}\n      onSelect={(point) => {\n        setSelectedId(point?.datum.id ?? null)\n      }}\n    />\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartPoint"},{"type":"text","value":" includes:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the original "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"datum"},{"type":"text","value":" and its original index;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"stable point and mark keys;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"group value and label;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"typed semantic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"xValue"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"yValue"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"optional interval endpoints and range-or-difference presentation hints;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"resolved pixel "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"resolved color."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read product values from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"point.datum"},{"type":"text","value":". Use pixel coordinates only to position\nan overlay."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"rich-and-nested-tooltips","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rich and nested tooltips"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Framework adapters can replace only the tooltip body while the shared host\ncontinues to own focus, ordering, anchoring, placement, portal coordinates,\nand dismissal. This React example places a nested pie beside the native rows:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Chart as TooltipChart } from '@tanstack/charts/react/tooltip'\n\nexport function RevenueChart() {\n  return (\n    <TooltipChart\n      definition={definition}\n      ariaLabel=\"Revenue by series\"\n      renderTooltipBody={({ points, defaultBody, pinned, dismiss }) => (\n        <div\n          style={{\n            display: 'grid',\n            gridTemplateColumns: 'auto 8rem',\n            gap: 12,\n          }}\n        >\n          <div>{defaultBody}</div>\n          <div>\n            <SeriesPie points={points} />\n            {pinned ? (\n              <button type=\"button\" onClick={dismiss}>\n                Close\n              </button>\n            ) : null}\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      )}\n    />\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The nested component is an ordinary chart built from the focused group:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import * as React from 'react'\nimport { defineChart, type ChartPoint } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { polar, radialArc } from '@tanstack/charts/polar'\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/react'\nimport { pie } from 'd3-shape'\n\ninterface RevenueRow {\n  date: Date\n  series: string\n  value: number\n}\n\ntype RevenuePoint = ChartPoint<RevenueRow, Date, number>\n\nfunction SeriesPie({ points }: { points: readonly RevenuePoint[] }) {\n  const pieDefinition = React.useMemo(() => {\n    const slices = pie<RevenuePoint>()\n      .sort(null)\n      .value((point) => Math.max(0, point.yValue))(points)\n\n    return defineChart({\n      marks: [\n        polar({\n          inset: 2,\n          marks: [\n            radialArc(slices, {\n              key: (slice) => slice.data.key,\n              fill: (slice) => slice.data.color ?? 'CanvasText',\n            }),\n          ],\n          scales: {\n            angle: null,\n            radius: null,\n          },\n        }),\n      ],\n      guides: false,\n      scales: {\n        x: null,\n        y: null,\n      },\n\n      keyboard: false,\n    })\n  }, [points])\n\n  return (\n    <Chart\n      definition={pieDefinition}\n      width={128}\n      height={96}\n      ariaLabel=\"Series share at the focused date\"\n    />\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultBody"},{"type":"text","value":" is the native title, rows, formatting, and swatches in the\nadapter's native composition form. Render it as-is, wrap it, or omit it.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"points"},{"type":"text","value":" preserves the grouped series order selected by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tooltip.sort"},{"type":"text","value":";\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"content"},{"type":"text","value":" exposes the same safe model when a different layout is needed.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pinned"},{"type":"text","value":" distinguishes transient inspection from interactive content, and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dismiss()"},{"type":"text","value":" clears the tooltip and returns focus to the chart when focus was\ninside the body."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A custom body is inert while transient, so a display-only nested chart can stay\nvisible but cannot receive pointer or keyboard input. Render controls only when\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pinned"},{"type":"text","value":" is true. The pinned body becomes a non-modal dialog; its controls\nstill need useful labels and intentional focus order. The adapter updates\nframework content with focused-point changes and unmounts it when the tooltip\nis dismissed or the parent chart unmounts."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For pin-only detail, configure "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"visibility: 'pinned'"},{"type":"text","value":" in the definition. The\nhost then suppresses both the transient shell and the adapter body instead of\nrequiring the framework renderer to return an empty element."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Native body composition"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React, Preact, Solid, Octane"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderTooltipBody"},{"type":"text","value":" prop"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"#tooltipBody"},{"type":"text","value":" scoped slot"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tooltipBody"},{"type":"text","value":" snippet prop"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Angular"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[tanstackChartTooltipBody]=\"definition\""},{"type":"text","value":" template"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lit"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.renderTooltipBody"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Alpine"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.renderTooltipBody"},{"type":"text","value":" returning DOM content"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each receives "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"points"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"content"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultBody"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pinned"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dismiss"},{"type":"text","value":".\nComposition stays beside the component, slot, template, or directive options;\nthe framework-neutral definition still owns every tooltip behavior."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"link","href":"../examples/interactive-charts.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interactive Charts examples"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../examples/polar-and-radar.md#pie-and-donut","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Polar and Radar Charts"}]},{"type":"text","value":" show the\ntwo pieces of the nested pie pattern."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"keyboard-behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keyboard behavior"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keyboard"},{"type":"text","value":" enabled:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"focusing the SVG selects the first navigable point;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Arrow keys move through the strategy's navigation order;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Home and End move to the first and last point;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enter or Space toggles an enabled sticky tooltip and calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSelect"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Escape dismisses a sticky tooltip."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A custom focus strategy owns both pointer resolution and navigation order.\nDo not supply a pointer-only strategy."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"dense-data","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dense data"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Linear nearest-point search is deliberately small. For many independently\nfocusable points, pass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartSpatialIndexFactory"},{"type":"text","value":" built with an optional\nspatial dependency. The factory also receives the resolved scene when it needs\nprimitive bounds rather than point anchors. The host rebuilds the index when\nthe scene changes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"./large-data.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Large Data"}]},{"type":"text","value":" before adding an index: when many rows share\nthe same pixels, a bounded representation is usually more useful than faster\nsearch over every raw point."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"ownership-checklist","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ownership checklist"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use chart-owned focus for datum inspection."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose two-dimensional, nearest-axis, or grouped-axis semantics explicitly."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep a finite distance unless continuous snapping is intended."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"crosshair"},{"type":"text","value":" for a single focus-driven guide; use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"whenFocused"},{"type":"text","value":" to reveal\nexisting data-bound geometry."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Share semantic cursor state through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChartCursor"},{"type":"text","value":", not copied pixels."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use native plaintext formatting for the 90% case."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"portal"},{"type":"text","value":" extension where clipped ancestors or stacking contexts can\nhide the tooltip."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the adapter's tooltip-body composition surface for framework content;\nuse focus callbacks for separate application-owned surfaces."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Give keyboard and pointer users equivalent state and selection."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep interactive content pinned and dismissible."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Let framework lifecycle destroy nested charts and external listeners with\ntheir owner."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"active-series","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Active series"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grouped tooltip rows follow their chart positions by default: top to bottom\nfor x focus, and left to right for y focus. The primary hovered or\nkeyboard-focused point gets a bold row with a shaded background in DOM tooltips, even when\nseveral series share a color."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For custom structured content, set each row's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"active"},{"type":"text","value":" field by comparing its\npoint with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context.primaryPoint"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"content: (points, context) => ({\n  rows: points.map((point) => ({\n    label: point.groupLabel,\n    value: context.formatY(point.yValue),\n    color: point.color,\n    active: point === context.primaryPoint,\n  })),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rows expose "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data-active=\"true\""},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data-active=\"false\""},{"type":"text","value":" for custom styling."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default emphasis uses CSS variables, so you can restyle it without\nreplacing the tooltip body. Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tooltip.className"},{"type":"text","value":" to scope the overrides:"}]},{"type":"code","value":".downloads-tooltip {\n  --ts-chart-tooltip-active-row-font-weight: 600;\n  --ts-chart-tooltip-active-row-background: transparent;\n  --ts-chart-tooltip-active-row-border-radius: 0;\n  --ts-chart-tooltip-active-row-shadow: none;\n}","lang":"css"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"active: false"},{"type":"text","value":" in custom structured content to disable the highlight.\nFor complete control over markup and styling, use your adapter's tooltip-body\ncomposition surface. Structured "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"content.rows"},{"type":"text","value":" retain their "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"active"},{"type":"text","value":" state\nfor your renderer to use. Body render callbacks also receive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"primaryPoint"},{"type":"text","value":",\nindependent of the sorted "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"points"},{"type":"text","value":" list."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"default-nearest-point","text":"Default nearest point","level":2},{"id":"axis-focus-modes","text":"Axis focus modes","level":2},{"id":"angular-focus","text":"Angular focus","level":2},{"id":"automatic-tooltip-mapping","text":"Automatic tooltip mapping","level":2},{"id":"tooltip-motion","text":"Tooltip motion","level":2},{"id":"application-owned-pointer-timing","text":"Application-owned pointer timing","level":2},{"id":"anchoring-and-placement","text":"Anchoring and placement","level":2},{"id":"escaping-clipped-containers","text":"Escaping clipped containers","level":2},{"id":"typed-callbacks","text":"Typed callbacks","level":2},{"id":"rich-and-nested-tooltips","text":"Rich and nested tooltips","level":2},{"id":"keyboard-behavior","text":"Keyboard behavior","level":2},{"id":"dense-data","text":"Dense data","level":2},{"id":"ownership-checklist","text":"Ownership checklist","level":2},{"id":"active-series","text":"Active series","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe DOM host provides a small automatic path for the common case:\n\n- find the nearest chart point;\n- draw a focus marker;\n- show locale-aware text;\n- expose the same point to pointer and keyboard users;\n- notify typed application callbacks.\n\nUse that path until the product needs richer interaction.\n\n## Default nearest point\n\nImport the built-in tooltip extension and add it to the definition:\n\n```ts\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\n\nconst interactiveDefinition = defineChart(definition, { tooltip })\n\nconst host = mountChart(element, {\n  definition: interactiveDefinition,\n  height: 320,\n  ariaLabel: 'Weekly downloads',\n})\n```\n\nThe default focus strategy resolves one nearest point in two dimensions.\n`maxFocusDistance` defaults to 48 scene pixels. Empty space farther from any\npoint clears transient focus.\n\n## Axis focus modes\n\n| Mode        | Result                                                                    |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| omitted     | One nearest painted geometry or point in two dimensions                   |\n| `nearest-x` | The containing mark, otherwise one point prioritizing x distance          |\n| `nearest-y` | The containing mark, otherwise one point prioritizing y distance          |\n| `group-x`   | The containing mark first, plus its semantic x group; otherwise nearest x |\n| `group-y`   | The containing mark first, plus its semantic y group; otherwise nearest y |\n\nGrouped focus is appropriate for comparing several series at the same date or\ncategory. A sparse snapped cursor can opt into\n`maxFocusDistance: Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY`; keep the finite default when\nempty space should mean no focus.\n\n## Angular focus\n\nUse `focusGroupAngle` for the radial equivalent of `group-x`:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineChart, type ChartDefinition } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { focusGroupAngle } from '@tanstack/charts/polar'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\n\ndeclare const radialDefinition: ChartDefinition\n\nconst interactiveDefinition = defineChart(radialDefinition, {\n  focus: focusGroupAngle,\n  tooltip,\n})\n```\n\nThe nearest radial ray selects the semantic angle, the closest radius becomes\nprimary, and the tooltip receives one point per series at that angle. The\nstrategy uses the same finite `maxFocusDistance` policy as axis grouping.\nOrdinary pie and donut charts can keep default nearest focus: `radialArc`\nattaches the exact painted slice geometry, including the donut hole.\n\nDefault `primary` and `group` presentation follows the canonical focused scene\npoints. Equal x/y/series values in another facet do not implicitly paint a\nsecond focus marker. To synchronize a visual cursor across facets without\nturning those mirrors into additional selected data, add an ordinary focus\nmark with `whenFocused(..., { match: 'x' })` or `match: 'y'`. The tooltip and\nfocus callback still receive the resolver's primary point or explicit focus\ngroup.\n\n```ts\nwhenFocused(bandX(rows, { x: 'date' }), { match: 'x' })\nwhenFocused(bandY(rows, { y: 'value' }), { match: 'y' })\n```\n\nThese are presentation filters, not alternate selection strategies. The first\npaints a vertical band wherever the focused x value exists; the second paints a\nhorizontal band wherever the focused y value exists. `whenFocused` can only\nreveal geometry already emitted by its authored mark. It cannot move one\nstable band between values.\n\nUse the data-less `crosshair` mark when one renderer-native guide should follow\nthe active focus instead of revealing authored geometry for a matching datum:\n\n```ts group=focused-crosshair env=charts file=/src/chart.ts entry\nimport { defineChart, lineY } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { crosshair } from '@tanstack/charts/crosshair'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\nimport { scalePoint } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/point'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\nimport { rows } from './data'\n\nexport default defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    lineY(rows, {\n      x: 'week',\n      y: 'value',\n      points: true,\n      stroke: '#2563eb',\n      strokeWidth: 2.5,\n    }),\n    crosshair({ x: { label: true }, y: false }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: () => scalePoint<string>().padding(0.2) },\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear, grid: true, axis: { label: 'Active users' } },\n  },\n\n  focus: 'nearest-x',\n  maxFocusDistance: Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY,\n  tooltip,\n})\n```\n\n```ts group=focused-crosshair file=/src/data.ts collapsed\nexport const rows = [\n  { week: 'May 4', value: 820 },\n  { week: 'May 11', value: 960 },\n  { week: 'May 18', value: 1_140 },\n  { week: 'May 25', value: 1_280 },\n  { week: 'Jun 1', value: 1_210 },\n  { week: 'Jun 8', value: 1_390 },\n]\n```\n\nThe vertical rule follows pointer and keyboard focus. The infinite distance is\nan explicit continuous-snapping policy; keep the finite default when empty\nspace should clear focus.\n\n`crosshair` defaults to both axis rules with no labels or marker. Setting\n`band: true` or a band options object replaces that axis rule; axes with zero\nbandwidth emit no band. Guides are clipped to the plot and labels are clamped\nto the surface. They do not change nearest-point selection, add hit targets,\nor suppress the primary focus ring. Use `focusRing: false` only when authored\ncursor geometry deliberately replaces the ring. See\n[Focus and Interaction](../reference/focus-and-interaction.md#crosshair-guides)\nfor the complete band paint contract and controlled cursor behavior.\n\n[Open the stacked cursor-band catalog case](https://tanstack.com/charts/catalog/119-stacked-bar-band-cursor/).\n\n## Automatic tooltip mapping\n\nThe default `tooltip` extension renders labeled rows for the focused point.\nGrouped focus uses the shared axis value as a heading and renders one row and\ncolor swatch per series. Visible axis labels carry into the tooltip. Numbers\nuse the user's locale and dates use stable UTC ISO formatting.\n\nRect and link endpoints display as ranges. Bars and areas with an explicit\nbaseline display the interval length, so a stacked segment reports its own\nvalue instead of the cumulative endpoint.\n\nOrder built-in channels, datum fields, and derived text for a single focused\npoint:\n\n```ts\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks,\n  scales: {\n    x: x,\n    y: y,\n  },\n\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    items: [\n      {\n        channel: 'y',\n        label: 'Revenue',\n        text: (point) => currency(point.yValue),\n      },\n      {\n        field: 'status',\n        label: 'Status',\n      },\n      {\n        id: 'change',\n        label: 'Change',\n        text: (point, { pinned }) =>\n          pinned && point.datum.change != null\n            ? percent(point.datum.change)\n            : null,\n      },\n      'x',\n    ],\n  },\n})\n```\n\nArray order is row order. A nullish field or `text` result omits the row.\nItem `text`, `content`, `format`, and `formatGroup` callbacks receive `pinned`,\nwhich is `false` during transient inspection and `true` after click, Enter, or\nSpace.\nUse it to keep the transient tooltip compact and reveal detailed rows when the\nsame tooltip is pinned.\nGrouped focus keeps its shared-axis heading and series rows. By default, rows\nfollow the marks top-to-bottom for an x-group and left-to-right for a y-group.\nOverride that with `sort: 'color-domain'`, `sort: 'focus'`, or a typed\ncomparator. Use channel items to format their heading, series names, and values.\nUse `content` when a grouped tooltip needs additional columns or nested\nsections.\n\nCustomize plaintext content with typed formatters:\n\n```ts\nconst formattedDefinition = defineChart(definition, {\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    format(point, { pinned }) {\n      const suffix = pinned ? ' · pinned' : ''\n      return `${point.datum.label}: ${point.datum.value.toLocaleString()}${suffix}`\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nFor grouped focus:\n\n```ts\nconst groupedDefinition = defineChart(definition, {\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    formatGroup(points, { pinned }) {\n      const date = points[0]?.xValue\n      const heading =\n        date instanceof Date ? date.toLocaleDateString() : String(date ?? '')\n\n      return [\n        pinned ? `${heading} · pinned` : heading,\n        ...points.map(\n          (point) =>\n            `${point.groupLabel}: ${point.datum.value.toLocaleString()}`,\n        ),\n      ].join('\\n')\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nFormatting precedence is `content`, `formatGroup`, `format`, then the automatic\ncontent. All three callbacks receive the same `ChartTooltipContentContext`.\n`content` returns safe title and row data. `format` and `formatGroup` return\nplain text; returning HTML does not create DOM.\n\nAdd `className` to style the native HTML surface. Clicking pins the current\ntooltip for text selection. A later click or Escape unpins it. Set\n`sticky: false` to disable pinning.\n\nSet `visibility: 'pinned'` when focus should style the chart without opening a\ntransient tooltip. Click, Enter, or Space can still pin the focused point; only\nthe pinned surface and adapter body are mounted. The default is\n`visibility: 'focus'`.\n\n## Tooltip motion\n\nThe built-in tooltip uses the active motion renderer's transition for entry,\nmovement between points, retargeting, and exit:\n\n```ts\nimport { motion } from '@tanstack/charts/motion'\n\nconst renderer = motion({\n  transition: {\n    type: 'spring',\n    stiffness: 170,\n    damping: 18,\n    mass: 1,\n  },\n})\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks,\n  scales: {\n    x: null,\n    y: null,\n  },\n  tooltip,\n})\n\nmountChartRenderer(container, {\n  definition,\n  renderer,\n  width: 640,\n  height: 360,\n  ariaLabel: 'Monthly visitors',\n})\n```\n\nA static chart-level transition can refine the renderer fallback:\n\n```ts\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks,\n  scales: {\n    x: null,\n    y: null,\n  },\n  motion: {\n    transition: { type: 'spring', stiffness: 170, damping: 18, mass: 1 },\n  },\n  tooltip,\n})\n```\n\nSet `tooltip.motion` to another transition to override both, or set it to\n`false` to keep the tooltip immediate. These options customize the active\nmotion renderer; a static renderer stays immediate and does not import spring\nphysics. The renderer's reduced-motion policy also applies to the tooltip.\n\nFor fast pointer inspection alongside slower data animation, set\n`tooltip: { use: tooltip, motion: false }`, or give the tooltip a short tween:\n\n```ts\nconst tooltipOptions = {\n  use: tooltip,\n  motion: { transition: { type: 'tween', duration: 120 } },\n}\n```\n\nInline mark `states` wait for active entrance and data motion to finish.\nTooltips and separate focus marks continue updating during that time. See\nthe [motion reference](../reference/motion.md#motion) for an immediate\n`whenFocused` dot example.\n\n## Application-owned pointer timing\n\nSet definition `pointer: false` when the application decides when inspection\nbegins, such as after a touch hold. Resolve the event and paint focus through\nthe controller exposed by `host.interaction` or `onRender`:\n\n```ts\nconst target = interaction.resolvePointer(event.clientX, event.clientY)\ninteraction.setControlledFocus(target)\n\n// On release or cancellation\ninteraction.setControlledFocus(null)\n```\n\nThis keeps focus marks and tooltip content in the definition. The controller\nuses presentation points, so an active path motion or viewport translation\ndoes not detach the focus marker and tooltip from the painted datum. See\n[Controlled point inspection](./interactions-and-selections.md#controlled-point-inspection)\nfor the complete ownership boundary.\n\n## Anchoring and placement\n\nPoint anchoring is the stable default for scatterplots, bars, and keyboard\nnavigation:\n\n```ts\nconst pointDefinition = defineChart(definition, {\n  tooltip: { use: tooltip, anchor: 'point', placement: 'top' },\n})\n```\n\nPointer anchoring is useful when a dense mark has a large interactive\nprimitive. Keyboard focus falls back to the primary point:\n\n```ts\nconst pointerDefinition = defineChart(definition, {\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    anchor: 'pointer',\n    placement: ['right', 'left', 'bottom', 'top'],\n    offset: 12,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nGrouped charts can avoid jumping between series by anchoring to the focused\ngroup's bounding-box center:\n\n```ts\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks,\n  scales: {\n    x: x,\n    y: y,\n  },\n\n  focus: 'group-x',\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    anchor: 'group-center',\n    placement: ['top', 'right', 'left', 'bottom'],\n    sort: 'color-domain',\n  },\n})\n```\n\nCoordinates can be selected independently. This follows the focused x value\nwhile fixing the tooltip to the top of the plot:\n\n```ts\nconst fixedYDefinition = defineChart(definition, {\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    anchor: { x: 'value', y: 'plot-top' },\n    placement: 'bottom',\n    offset: 12,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nA custom resolver covers event ranges, maps, and application-specific\nreference positions:\n\n```ts\nconst customAnchorDefinition = defineChart(definition, {\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    anchor: (_points, { focus, pointer, plot, surface, scales }) => ({\n      x: (scales.x.viewport?.map ?? scales.x.map)(focus.primary.xValue),\n      y: plot.y,\n    }),\n    placement: 'bottom-left',\n  },\n})\n```\n\nResolvers receive complete focus, pointer, plot, surface, and resolved-scale\nstate. Resolvers and placement use scene pixels. A nullish or non-finite custom\nanchor falls back to the primary point. A placement list uses the first fit,\nthen the least-overflowing candidate.\n\n## Escaping clipped containers\n\nKeep tooltip layering with the chart definition:\n\n```ts\nimport { portal } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip/portal'\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks,\n  scales: {\n    x: x,\n    y: y,\n  },\n\n  focus: 'group-x',\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    portal,\n    anchor: 'group-center',\n    placement: ['right', 'left', 'bottom', 'top'],\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThe `portal` extension opens the tooltip as a manual Popover in the browser top\nlayer where supported. It remains a DOM descendant of the chart, so inherited\nstyles, ancestor selectors, and chart-scoped CSS custom properties continue to\nwork. If Popover is unavailable or fails, the host moves the tooltip directly\nunder the chart's `ownerDocument` body with fixed high-stack positioning. Both\npaths escape `overflow: hidden` and local stacking contexts, use viewport\ncollision bounds, and reposition after scroll, viewport resize, or content\nresize. Omitting `portal` keeps ordinary absolute positioning inside the chart.\n\nFor consistent fallback styling, target `tooltip.className` from a\ndocument-level stylesheet and define required CSS custom properties on that\nclass or a shared document ancestor.\n\n## Typed callbacks\n\nUse callbacks when application UI needs the current semantic state:\n\n```tsx\nfunction WeeklyDownloads() {\n  const groupedDefinition = defineChart(definition, { focus: 'group-x' })\n\n  return (\n    <Chart\n      definition={groupedDefinition}\n      ariaLabel=\"Weekly downloads\"\n      onFocusChange={(point) => {\n        setFocusedRow(point?.datum ?? null)\n      }}\n      onFocusGroupChange={(points) => {\n        setFocusedRows(points.map((point) => point.datum))\n      }}\n      onSelect={(point) => {\n        setSelectedId(point?.datum.id ?? null)\n      }}\n    />\n  )\n}\n```\n\n`ChartPoint` includes:\n\n- the original `datum` and its original index;\n- stable point and mark keys;\n- group value and label;\n- typed semantic `xValue` and `yValue`;\n- optional interval endpoints and range-or-difference presentation hints;\n- resolved pixel `x` and `y`;\n- resolved color.\n\nRead product values from `point.datum`. Use pixel coordinates only to position\nan overlay.\n\n## Rich and nested tooltips\n\nFramework adapters can replace only the tooltip body while the shared host\ncontinues to own focus, ordering, anchoring, placement, portal coordinates,\nand dismissal. This React example places a nested pie beside the native rows:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Chart as TooltipChart } from '@tanstack/charts/react/tooltip'\n\nexport function RevenueChart() {\n  return (\n    <TooltipChart\n      definition={definition}\n      ariaLabel=\"Revenue by series\"\n      renderTooltipBody={({ points, defaultBody, pinned, dismiss }) => (\n        <div\n          style={{\n            display: 'grid',\n            gridTemplateColumns: 'auto 8rem',\n            gap: 12,\n          }}\n        >\n          <div>{defaultBody}</div>\n          <div>\n            <SeriesPie points={points} />\n            {pinned ? (\n              <button type=\"button\" onClick={dismiss}>\n                Close\n              </button>\n            ) : null}\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      )}\n    />\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe nested component is an ordinary chart built from the focused group:\n\n```tsx\nimport * as React from 'react'\nimport { defineChart, type ChartPoint } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { polar, radialArc } from '@tanstack/charts/polar'\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/react'\nimport { pie } from 'd3-shape'\n\ninterface RevenueRow {\n  date: Date\n  series: string\n  value: number\n}\n\ntype RevenuePoint = ChartPoint<RevenueRow, Date, number>\n\nfunction SeriesPie({ points }: { points: readonly RevenuePoint[] }) {\n  const pieDefinition = React.useMemo(() => {\n    const slices = pie<RevenuePoint>()\n      .sort(null)\n      .value((point) => Math.max(0, point.yValue))(points)\n\n    return defineChart({\n      marks: [\n        polar({\n          inset: 2,\n          marks: [\n            radialArc(slices, {\n              key: (slice) => slice.data.key,\n              fill: (slice) => slice.data.color ?? 'CanvasText',\n            }),\n          ],\n          scales: {\n            angle: null,\n            radius: null,\n          },\n        }),\n      ],\n      guides: false,\n      scales: {\n        x: null,\n        y: null,\n      },\n\n      keyboard: false,\n    })\n  }, [points])\n\n  return (\n    <Chart\n      definition={pieDefinition}\n      width={128}\n      height={96}\n      ariaLabel=\"Series share at the focused date\"\n    />\n  )\n}\n```\n\n`defaultBody` is the native title, rows, formatting, and swatches in the\nadapter's native composition form. Render it as-is, wrap it, or omit it.\n`points` preserves the grouped series order selected by `tooltip.sort`;\n`content` exposes the same safe model when a different layout is needed.\n`pinned` distinguishes transient inspection from interactive content, and\n`dismiss()` clears the tooltip and returns focus to the chart when focus was\ninside the body.\n\nA custom body is inert while transient, so a display-only nested chart can stay\nvisible but cannot receive pointer or keyboard input. Render controls only when\n`pinned` is true. The pinned body becomes a non-modal dialog; its controls\nstill need useful labels and intentional focus order. The adapter updates\nframework content with focused-point changes and unmounts it when the tooltip\nis dismissed or the parent chart unmounts.\n\nFor pin-only detail, configure `visibility: 'pinned'` in the definition. The\nhost then suppresses both the transient shell and the adapter body instead of\nrequiring the framework renderer to return an empty element.\n\n| Adapter                      | Native body composition                            |\n| ---------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| React, Preact, Solid, Octane | `renderTooltipBody` prop                           |\n| Vue                          | `#tooltipBody` scoped slot                         |\n| Svelte                       | `tooltipBody` snippet prop                         |\n| Angular                      | `[tanstackChartTooltipBody]=\"definition\"` template |\n| Lit                          | `options.renderTooltipBody`                        |\n| Alpine                       | `options.renderTooltipBody` returning DOM content  |\n\nEach receives `points`, `content`, `defaultBody`, `pinned`, and `dismiss`.\nComposition stays beside the component, slot, template, or directive options;\nthe framework-neutral definition still owns every tooltip behavior.\n\nThe [Interactive Charts examples](../examples/interactive-charts.md) and\n[Polar and Radar Charts](../examples/polar-and-radar.md#pie-and-donut) show the\ntwo pieces of the nested pie pattern.\n\n## Keyboard behavior\n\nWith `keyboard` enabled:\n\n- focusing the SVG selects the first navigable point;\n- Arrow keys move through the strategy's navigation order;\n- Home and End move to the first and last point;\n- Enter or Space toggles an enabled sticky tooltip and calls `onSelect`;\n- Escape dismisses a sticky tooltip.\n\nA custom focus strategy owns both pointer resolution and navigation order.\nDo not supply a pointer-only strategy.\n\n## Dense data\n\nLinear nearest-point search is deliberately small. For many independently\nfocusable points, pass a `ChartSpatialIndexFactory` built with an optional\nspatial dependency. The factory also receives the resolved scene when it needs\nprimitive bounds rather than point anchors. The host rebuilds the index when\nthe scene changes.\n\nSee [Large Data](./large-data.md) before adding an index: when many rows share\nthe same pixels, a bounded representation is usually more useful than faster\nsearch over every raw point.\n\n## Ownership checklist\n\n- Use chart-owned focus for datum inspection.\n- Choose two-dimensional, nearest-axis, or grouped-axis semantics explicitly.\n- Keep a finite distance unless continuous snapping is intended.\n- Use `crosshair` for a single focus-driven guide; use `whenFocused` to reveal\n  existing data-bound geometry.\n- Share semantic cursor state through `createChartCursor`, not copied pixels.\n- Use native plaintext formatting for the 90% case.\n- Use the `portal` extension where clipped ancestors or stacking contexts can\n  hide the tooltip.\n- Use the adapter's tooltip-body composition surface for framework content;\n  use focus callbacks for separate application-owned surfaces.\n- Give keyboard and pointer users equivalent state and selection.\n- Keep interactive content pinned and dismissible.\n- Let framework lifecycle destroy nested charts and external listeners with\n  their owner.\n\n### Active series\n\nGrouped tooltip rows follow their chart positions by default: top to bottom\nfor x focus, and left to right for y focus. The primary hovered or\nkeyboard-focused point gets a bold row with a shaded background in DOM tooltips, even when\nseveral series share a color.\n\nFor custom structured content, set each row's `active` field by comparing its\npoint with `context.primaryPoint`:\n\n```ts\ncontent: (points, context) => ({\n  rows: points.map((point) => ({\n    label: point.groupLabel,\n    value: context.formatY(point.yValue),\n    color: point.color,\n    active: point === context.primaryPoint,\n  })),\n})\n```\n\nRows expose `data-active=\"true\"` or `data-active=\"false\"` for custom styling.\n\nThe default emphasis uses CSS variables, so you can restyle it without\nreplacing the tooltip body. Set `tooltip.className` to scope the overrides:\n\n```css\n.downloads-tooltip {\n  --ts-chart-tooltip-active-row-font-weight: 600;\n  --ts-chart-tooltip-active-row-background: transparent;\n  --ts-chart-tooltip-active-row-border-radius: 0;\n  --ts-chart-tooltip-active-row-shadow: none;\n}\n```\n\nSet `active: false` in custom structured content to disable the highlight.\nFor complete control over markup and styling, use your adapter's tooltip-body\ncomposition surface. Structured `content.rows` retain their `active` state\nfor your renderer to use. Body render callbacks also receive `primaryPoint`,\nindependent of the sorted `points` list.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Tooltips and Focus\ndescription: Configure grouped focus, crosshairs, automatic content, ordering, placement, portaling, pinning, and framework-composed tooltip bodies.\n---\n\nThe DOM host provides a small automatic path for the common case:\n\n- find the nearest chart point;\n- draw a focus marker;\n- show locale-aware text;\n- expose the same point to pointer and keyboard users;\n- notify typed application callbacks.\n\nUse that path until the product needs richer interaction.\n\n## Default nearest point\n\nImport the built-in tooltip extension and add it to the definition:\n\n```ts\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\n\nconst interactiveDefinition = defineChart(definition, { tooltip })\n\nconst host = mountChart(element, {\n  definition: interactiveDefinition,\n  height: 320,\n  ariaLabel: 'Weekly downloads',\n})\n```\n\nThe default focus strategy resolves one nearest point in two dimensions.\n`maxFocusDistance` defaults to 48 scene pixels. Empty space farther from any\npoint clears transient focus.\n\n## Axis focus modes\n\n| Mode        | Result                                                                    |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| omitted     | One nearest painted geometry or point in two dimensions                   |\n| `nearest-x` | The containing mark, otherwise one point prioritizing x distance          |\n| `nearest-y` | The containing mark, otherwise one point prioritizing y distance          |\n| `group-x`   | The containing mark first, plus its semantic x group; otherwise nearest x |\n| `group-y`   | The containing mark first, plus its semantic y group; otherwise nearest y |\n\nGrouped focus is appropriate for comparing several series at the same date or\ncategory. A sparse snapped cursor can opt into\n`maxFocusDistance: Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY`; keep the finite default when\nempty space should mean no focus.\n\n## Angular focus\n\nUse `focusGroupAngle` for the radial equivalent of `group-x`:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineChart, type ChartDefinition } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { focusGroupAngle } from '@tanstack/charts/polar'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\n\ndeclare const radialDefinition: ChartDefinition\n\nconst interactiveDefinition = defineChart(radialDefinition, {\n  focus: focusGroupAngle,\n  tooltip,\n})\n```\n\nThe nearest radial ray selects the semantic angle, the closest radius becomes\nprimary, and the tooltip receives one point per series at that angle. The\nstrategy uses the same finite `maxFocusDistance` policy as axis grouping.\nOrdinary pie and donut charts can keep default nearest focus: `radialArc`\nattaches the exact painted slice geometry, including the donut hole.\n\nDefault `primary` and `group` presentation follows the canonical focused scene\npoints. Equal x/y/series values in another facet do not implicitly paint a\nsecond focus marker. To synchronize a visual cursor across facets without\nturning those mirrors into additional selected data, add an ordinary focus\nmark with `whenFocused(..., { match: 'x' })` or `match: 'y'`. The tooltip and\nfocus callback still receive the resolver's primary point or explicit focus\ngroup.\n\n```ts\nwhenFocused(bandX(rows, { x: 'date' }), { match: 'x' })\nwhenFocused(bandY(rows, { y: 'value' }), { match: 'y' })\n```\n\nThese are presentation filters, not alternate selection strategies. The first\npaints a vertical band wherever the focused x value exists; the second paints a\nhorizontal band wherever the focused y value exists. `whenFocused` can only\nreveal geometry already emitted by its authored mark. It cannot move one\nstable band between values.\n\nUse the data-less `crosshair` mark when one renderer-native guide should follow\nthe active focus instead of revealing authored geometry for a matching datum:\n\n```ts group=focused-crosshair env=charts file=/src/chart.ts entry\nimport { defineChart, lineY } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { crosshair } from '@tanstack/charts/crosshair'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\nimport { scalePoint } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/point'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\nimport { rows } from './data'\n\nexport default defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    lineY(rows, {\n      x: 'week',\n      y: 'value',\n      points: true,\n      stroke: '#2563eb',\n      strokeWidth: 2.5,\n    }),\n    crosshair({ x: { label: true }, y: false }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: () => scalePoint<string>().padding(0.2) },\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear, grid: true, axis: { label: 'Active users' } },\n  },\n\n  focus: 'nearest-x',\n  maxFocusDistance: Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY,\n  tooltip,\n})\n```\n\n```ts group=focused-crosshair file=/src/data.ts collapsed\nexport const rows = [\n  { week: 'May 4', value: 820 },\n  { week: 'May 11', value: 960 },\n  { week: 'May 18', value: 1_140 },\n  { week: 'May 25', value: 1_280 },\n  { week: 'Jun 1', value: 1_210 },\n  { week: 'Jun 8', value: 1_390 },\n]\n```\n\nThe vertical rule follows pointer and keyboard focus. The infinite distance is\nan explicit continuous-snapping policy; keep the finite default when empty\nspace should clear focus.\n\n`crosshair` defaults to both axis rules with no labels or marker. Setting\n`band: true` or a band options object replaces that axis rule; axes with zero\nbandwidth emit no band. Guides are clipped to the plot and labels are clamped\nto the surface. They do not change nearest-point selection, add hit targets,\nor suppress the primary focus ring. Use `focusRing: false` only when authored\ncursor geometry deliberately replaces the ring. See\n[Focus and Interaction](../reference/focus-and-interaction.md#crosshair-guides)\nfor the complete band paint contract and controlled cursor behavior.\n\n[Open the stacked cursor-band catalog case](https://tanstack.com/charts/catalog/119-stacked-bar-band-cursor/).\n\n## Automatic tooltip mapping\n\nThe default `tooltip` extension renders labeled rows for the focused point.\nGrouped focus uses the shared axis value as a heading and renders one row and\ncolor swatch per series. Visible axis labels carry into the tooltip. Numbers\nuse the user's locale and dates use stable UTC ISO formatting.\n\nRect and link endpoints display as ranges. Bars and areas with an explicit\nbaseline display the interval length, so a stacked segment reports its own\nvalue instead of the cumulative endpoint.\n\nOrder built-in channels, datum fields, and derived text for a single focused\npoint:\n\n```ts\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks,\n  scales: {\n    x: x,\n    y: y,\n  },\n\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    items: [\n      {\n        channel: 'y',\n        label: 'Revenue',\n        text: (point) => currency(point.yValue),\n      },\n      {\n        field: 'status',\n        label: 'Status',\n      },\n      {\n        id: 'change',\n        label: 'Change',\n        text: (point, { pinned }) =>\n          pinned && point.datum.change != null\n            ? percent(point.datum.change)\n            : null,\n      },\n      'x',\n    ],\n  },\n})\n```\n\nArray order is row order. A nullish field or `text` result omits the row.\nItem `text`, `content`, `format`, and `formatGroup` callbacks receive `pinned`,\nwhich is `false` during transient inspection and `true` after click, Enter, or\nSpace.\nUse it to keep the transient tooltip compact and reveal detailed rows when the\nsame tooltip is pinned.\nGrouped focus keeps its shared-axis heading and series rows. By default, rows\nfollow the marks top-to-bottom for an x-group and left-to-right for a y-group.\nOverride that with `sort: 'color-domain'`, `sort: 'focus'`, or a typed\ncomparator. Use channel items to format their heading, series names, and values.\nUse `content` when a grouped tooltip needs additional columns or nested\nsections.\n\nCustomize plaintext content with typed formatters:\n\n```ts\nconst formattedDefinition = defineChart(definition, {\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    format(point, { pinned }) {\n      const suffix = pinned ? ' · pinned' : ''\n      return `${point.datum.label}: ${point.datum.value.toLocaleString()}${suffix}`\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nFor grouped focus:\n\n```ts\nconst groupedDefinition = defineChart(definition, {\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    formatGroup(points, { pinned }) {\n      const date = points[0]?.xValue\n      const heading =\n        date instanceof Date ? date.toLocaleDateString() : String(date ?? '')\n\n      return [\n        pinned ? `${heading} · pinned` : heading,\n        ...points.map(\n          (point) =>\n            `${point.groupLabel}: ${point.datum.value.toLocaleString()}`,\n        ),\n      ].join('\\n')\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nFormatting precedence is `content`, `formatGroup`, `format`, then the automatic\ncontent. All three callbacks receive the same `ChartTooltipContentContext`.\n`content` returns safe title and row data. `format` and `formatGroup` return\nplain text; returning HTML does not create DOM.\n\nAdd `className` to style the native HTML surface. Clicking pins the current\ntooltip for text selection. A later click or Escape unpins it. Set\n`sticky: false` to disable pinning.\n\nSet `visibility: 'pinned'` when focus should style the chart without opening a\ntransient tooltip. Click, Enter, or Space can still pin the focused point; only\nthe pinned surface and adapter body are mounted. The default is\n`visibility: 'focus'`.\n\n## Tooltip motion\n\nThe built-in tooltip uses the active motion renderer's transition for entry,\nmovement between points, retargeting, and exit:\n\n```ts\nimport { motion } from '@tanstack/charts/motion'\n\nconst renderer = motion({\n  transition: {\n    type: 'spring',\n    stiffness: 170,\n    damping: 18,\n    mass: 1,\n  },\n})\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks,\n  scales: {\n    x: null,\n    y: null,\n  },\n  tooltip,\n})\n\nmountChartRenderer(container, {\n  definition,\n  renderer,\n  width: 640,\n  height: 360,\n  ariaLabel: 'Monthly visitors',\n})\n```\n\nA static chart-level transition can refine the renderer fallback:\n\n```ts\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks,\n  scales: {\n    x: null,\n    y: null,\n  },\n  motion: {\n    transition: { type: 'spring', stiffness: 170, damping: 18, mass: 1 },\n  },\n  tooltip,\n})\n```\n\nSet `tooltip.motion` to another transition to override both, or set it to\n`false` to keep the tooltip immediate. These options customize the active\nmotion renderer; a static renderer stays immediate and does not import spring\nphysics. The renderer's reduced-motion policy also applies to the tooltip.\n\nFor fast pointer inspection alongside slower data animation, set\n`tooltip: { use: tooltip, motion: false }`, or give the tooltip a short tween:\n\n```ts\nconst tooltipOptions = {\n  use: tooltip,\n  motion: { transition: { type: 'tween', duration: 120 } },\n}\n```\n\nInline mark `states` wait for active entrance and data motion to finish.\nTooltips and separate focus marks continue updating during that time. See\nthe [motion reference](../reference/motion.md#motion) for an immediate\n`whenFocused` dot example.\n\n## Application-owned pointer timing\n\nSet definition `pointer: false` when the application decides when inspection\nbegins, such as after a touch hold. Resolve the event and paint focus through\nthe controller exposed by `host.interaction` or `onRender`:\n\n```ts\nconst target = interaction.resolvePointer(event.clientX, event.clientY)\ninteraction.setControlledFocus(target)\n\n// On release or cancellation\ninteraction.setControlledFocus(null)\n```\n\nThis keeps focus marks and tooltip content in the definition. The controller\nuses presentation points, so an active path motion or viewport translation\ndoes not detach the focus marker and tooltip from the painted datum. See\n[Controlled point inspection](./interactions-and-selections.md#controlled-point-inspection)\nfor the complete ownership boundary.\n\n## Anchoring and placement\n\nPoint anchoring is the stable default for scatterplots, bars, and keyboard\nnavigation:\n\n```ts\nconst pointDefinition = defineChart(definition, {\n  tooltip: { use: tooltip, anchor: 'point', placement: 'top' },\n})\n```\n\nPointer anchoring is useful when a dense mark has a large interactive\nprimitive. Keyboard focus falls back to the primary point:\n\n```ts\nconst pointerDefinition = defineChart(definition, {\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    anchor: 'pointer',\n    placement: ['right', 'left', 'bottom', 'top'],\n    offset: 12,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nGrouped charts can avoid jumping between series by anchoring to the focused\ngroup's bounding-box center:\n\n```ts\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks,\n  scales: {\n    x: x,\n    y: y,\n  },\n\n  focus: 'group-x',\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    anchor: 'group-center',\n    placement: ['top', 'right', 'left', 'bottom'],\n    sort: 'color-domain',\n  },\n})\n```\n\nCoordinates can be selected independently. This follows the focused x value\nwhile fixing the tooltip to the top of the plot:\n\n```ts\nconst fixedYDefinition = defineChart(definition, {\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    anchor: { x: 'value', y: 'plot-top' },\n    placement: 'bottom',\n    offset: 12,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nA custom resolver covers event ranges, maps, and application-specific\nreference positions:\n\n```ts\nconst customAnchorDefinition = defineChart(definition, {\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    anchor: (_points, { focus, pointer, plot, surface, scales }) => ({\n      x: (scales.x.viewport?.map ?? scales.x.map)(focus.primary.xValue),\n      y: plot.y,\n    }),\n    placement: 'bottom-left',\n  },\n})\n```\n\nResolvers receive complete focus, pointer, plot, surface, and resolved-scale\nstate. Resolvers and placement use scene pixels. A nullish or non-finite custom\nanchor falls back to the primary point. A placement list uses the first fit,\nthen the least-overflowing candidate.\n\n## Escaping clipped containers\n\nKeep tooltip layering with the chart definition:\n\n```ts\nimport { portal } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip/portal'\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks,\n  scales: {\n    x: x,\n    y: y,\n  },\n\n  focus: 'group-x',\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    portal,\n    anchor: 'group-center',\n    placement: ['right', 'left', 'bottom', 'top'],\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThe `portal` extension opens the tooltip as a manual Popover in the browser top\nlayer where supported. It remains a DOM descendant of the chart, so inherited\nstyles, ancestor selectors, and chart-scoped CSS custom properties continue to\nwork. If Popover is unavailable or fails, the host moves the tooltip directly\nunder the chart's `ownerDocument` body with fixed high-stack positioning. Both\npaths escape `overflow: hidden` and local stacking contexts, use viewport\ncollision bounds, and reposition after scroll, viewport resize, or content\nresize. Omitting `portal` keeps ordinary absolute positioning inside the chart.\n\nFor consistent fallback styling, target `tooltip.className` from a\ndocument-level stylesheet and define required CSS custom properties on that\nclass or a shared document ancestor.\n\n## Typed callbacks\n\nUse callbacks when application UI needs the current semantic state:\n\n```tsx\nfunction WeeklyDownloads() {\n  const groupedDefinition = defineChart(definition, { focus: 'group-x' })\n\n  return (\n    <Chart\n      definition={groupedDefinition}\n      ariaLabel=\"Weekly downloads\"\n      onFocusChange={(point) => {\n        setFocusedRow(point?.datum ?? null)\n      }}\n      onFocusGroupChange={(points) => {\n        setFocusedRows(points.map((point) => point.datum))\n      }}\n      onSelect={(point) => {\n        setSelectedId(point?.datum.id ?? null)\n      }}\n    />\n  )\n}\n```\n\n`ChartPoint` includes:\n\n- the original `datum` and its original index;\n- stable point and mark keys;\n- group value and label;\n- typed semantic `xValue` and `yValue`;\n- optional interval endpoints and range-or-difference presentation hints;\n- resolved pixel `x` and `y`;\n- resolved color.\n\nRead product values from `point.datum`. Use pixel coordinates only to position\nan overlay.\n\n## Rich and nested tooltips\n\nFramework adapters can replace only the tooltip body while the shared host\ncontinues to own focus, ordering, anchoring, placement, portal coordinates,\nand dismissal. This React example places a nested pie beside the native rows:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Chart as TooltipChart } from '@tanstack/charts/react/tooltip'\n\nexport function RevenueChart() {\n  return (\n    <TooltipChart\n      definition={definition}\n      ariaLabel=\"Revenue by series\"\n      renderTooltipBody={({ points, defaultBody, pinned, dismiss }) => (\n        <div\n          style={{\n            display: 'grid',\n            gridTemplateColumns: 'auto 8rem',\n            gap: 12,\n          }}\n        >\n          <div>{defaultBody}</div>\n          <div>\n            <SeriesPie points={points} />\n            {pinned ? (\n              <button type=\"button\" onClick={dismiss}>\n                Close\n              </button>\n            ) : null}\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      )}\n    />\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe nested component is an ordinary chart built from the focused group:\n\n```tsx\nimport * as React from 'react'\nimport { defineChart, type ChartPoint } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { polar, radialArc } from '@tanstack/charts/polar'\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/react'\nimport { pie } from 'd3-shape'\n\ninterface RevenueRow {\n  date: Date\n  series: string\n  value: number\n}\n\ntype RevenuePoint = ChartPoint<RevenueRow, Date, number>\n\nfunction SeriesPie({ points }: { points: readonly RevenuePoint[] }) {\n  const pieDefinition = React.useMemo(() => {\n    const slices = pie<RevenuePoint>()\n      .sort(null)\n      .value((point) => Math.max(0, point.yValue))(points)\n\n    return defineChart({\n      marks: [\n        polar({\n          inset: 2,\n          marks: [\n            radialArc(slices, {\n              key: (slice) => slice.data.key,\n              fill: (slice) => slice.data.color ?? 'CanvasText',\n            }),\n          ],\n          scales: {\n            angle: null,\n            radius: null,\n          },\n        }),\n      ],\n      guides: false,\n      scales: {\n        x: null,\n        y: null,\n      },\n\n      keyboard: false,\n    })\n  }, [points])\n\n  return (\n    <Chart\n      definition={pieDefinition}\n      width={128}\n      height={96}\n      ariaLabel=\"Series share at the focused date\"\n    />\n  )\n}\n```\n\n`defaultBody` is the native title, rows, formatting, and swatches in the\nadapter's native composition form. Render it as-is, wrap it, or omit it.\n`points` preserves the grouped series order selected by `tooltip.sort`;\n`content` exposes the same safe model when a different layout is needed.\n`pinned` distinguishes transient inspection from interactive content, and\n`dismiss()` clears the tooltip and returns focus to the chart when focus was\ninside the body.\n\nA custom body is inert while transient, so a display-only nested chart can stay\nvisible but cannot receive pointer or keyboard input. Render controls only when\n`pinned` is true. The pinned body becomes a non-modal dialog; its controls\nstill need useful labels and intentional focus order. The adapter updates\nframework content with focused-point changes and unmounts it when the tooltip\nis dismissed or the parent chart unmounts.\n\nFor pin-only detail, configure `visibility: 'pinned'` in the definition. The\nhost then suppresses both the transient shell and the adapter body instead of\nrequiring the framework renderer to return an empty element.\n\n| Adapter                      | Native body composition                            |\n| ---------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| React, Preact, Solid, Octane | `renderTooltipBody` prop                           |\n| Vue                          | `#tooltipBody` scoped slot                         |\n| Svelte                       | `tooltipBody` snippet prop                         |\n| Angular                      | `[tanstackChartTooltipBody]=\"definition\"` template |\n| Lit                          | `options.renderTooltipBody`                        |\n| Alpine                       | `options.renderTooltipBody` returning DOM content  |\n\nEach receives `points`, `content`, `defaultBody`, `pinned`, and `dismiss`.\nComposition stays beside the component, slot, template, or directive options;\nthe framework-neutral definition still owns every tooltip behavior.\n\nThe [Interactive Charts examples](../examples/interactive-charts.md) and\n[Polar and Radar Charts](../examples/polar-and-radar.md#pie-and-donut) show the\ntwo pieces of the nested pie pattern.\n\n## Keyboard behavior\n\nWith `keyboard` enabled:\n\n- focusing the SVG selects the first navigable point;\n- Arrow keys move through the strategy's navigation order;\n- Home and End move to the first and last point;\n- Enter or Space toggles an enabled sticky tooltip and calls `onSelect`;\n- Escape dismisses a sticky tooltip.\n\nA custom focus strategy owns both pointer resolution and navigation order.\nDo not supply a pointer-only strategy.\n\n## Dense data\n\nLinear nearest-point search is deliberately small. For many independently\nfocusable points, pass a `ChartSpatialIndexFactory` built with an optional\nspatial dependency. The factory also receives the resolved scene when it needs\nprimitive bounds rather than point anchors. The host rebuilds the index when\nthe scene changes.\n\nSee [Large Data](./large-data.md) before adding an index: when many rows share\nthe same pixels, a bounded representation is usually more useful than faster\nsearch over every raw point.\n\n## Ownership checklist\n\n- Use chart-owned focus for datum inspection.\n- Choose two-dimensional, nearest-axis, or grouped-axis semantics explicitly.\n- Keep a finite distance unless continuous snapping is intended.\n- Use `crosshair` for a single focus-driven guide; use `whenFocused` to reveal\n  existing data-bound geometry.\n- Share semantic cursor state through `createChartCursor`, not copied pixels.\n- Use native plaintext formatting for the 90% case.\n- Use the `portal` extension where clipped ancestors or stacking contexts can\n  hide the tooltip.\n- Use the adapter's tooltip-body composition surface for framework content;\n  use focus callbacks for separate application-owned surfaces.\n- Give keyboard and pointer users equivalent state and selection.\n- Keep interactive content pinned and dismissible.\n- Let framework lifecycle destroy nested charts and external listeners with\n  their owner.\n\n### Active series\n\nGrouped tooltip rows follow their chart positions by default: top to bottom\nfor x focus, and left to right for y focus. The primary hovered or\nkeyboard-focused point gets a bold row with a shaded background in DOM tooltips, even when\nseveral series share a color.\n\nFor custom structured content, set each row's `active` field by comparing its\npoint with `context.primaryPoint`:\n\n```ts\ncontent: (points, context) => ({\n  rows: points.map((point) => ({\n    label: point.groupLabel,\n    value: context.formatY(point.yValue),\n    color: point.color,\n    active: point === context.primaryPoint,\n  })),\n})\n```\n\nRows expose `data-active=\"true\"` or `data-active=\"false\"` for custom styling.\n\nThe default emphasis uses CSS variables, so you can restyle it without\nreplacing the tooltip body. Set `tooltip.className` to scope the overrides:\n\n```css\n.downloads-tooltip {\n  --ts-chart-tooltip-active-row-font-weight: 600;\n  --ts-chart-tooltip-active-row-background: transparent;\n  --ts-chart-tooltip-active-row-border-radius: 0;\n  --ts-chart-tooltip-active-row-shadow: none;\n}\n```\n\nSet `active: false` in custom structured content to disable the highlight.\nFor complete control over markup and styling, use your adapter's tooltip-body\ncomposition surface. Structured `content.rows` retain their `active` state\nfor your renderer to use. Body render callbacks also receive `primaryPoint`,\nindependent of the sorted `points` list.\n"}
